# Source is always text for diff and grep purposes.
#
# Git decides binary-ness by looking for a NUL in the first 8000 bytes. A source
# file that legitimately holds one — a composite-key separator written as a raw
# byte rather than the escape `\0` — is then excluded from every content-bearing
# diff and grep, silently. That happened here: `scripts/roll-cap-sweep.mjs` went
# into the repo as `Bin 0 -> 7316 bytes`, and none of the three commits that
# touched it ever showed a line (#1282).
#
# `diff` is deliberate, and `text` is deliberately absent: this marks the paths
# readable without enabling end-of-line normalisation, which would rewrite
# working trees across the repo for a problem that is only about display.
*.ts    diff
*.tsx   diff
*.mjs   diff
*.cjs   diff
*.js    diff
*.jsx   diff
*.json  diff
*.md    diff
*.css   diff
*.html  diff
*.yml   diff
*.yaml  diff
